- Create a list for the results.
- Check if the current node exists.
- Process the left subtree first.
- Then, process the right subtree.
- Only after that, add the value of the current node.
- Return the list.
Time Complexity: O(n)

The algorithm visits each node exactly once. Therefore, it requires O(n) time for n nodes.

Space Complexity: O(n) in the worst case, accounting for the result list and the recursion stack.

Possible improvement: An iterative solution can be implemented using a stack. However, the time complexity will remain O(n).
